package cajeta.gpu.core;

/**
 * Storage format of a {@link Texture2D}. Selects how texels are stored on the
 * device (channel count + per-channel encoding); a `Texture2D.sample(...)`
 * always returns a `Vector<float32, 4>` regardless — the hardware sampler
 * expands missing channels (G/B = 0, A = 1) and decodes the stored encoding to
 * float.
 *
 * Two independent axes are folded into one format:
 *   - **channels:** 1 (R) or 4 (RGBA).
 *   - **encoding:** 32-bit float (the value is read back as-is, any range),
 *     16-bit half float (the cheap-HDR encoding — half the bandwidth of f32,
 *     read back as float), or 8-bit UNORM (a byte 0..255 stored, read back
 *     normalized to float [0, 1] — the common, compact color-texture encoding).
 *
 * `upload(float32[])` always takes channel-interleaved floats in [0, 1] for the
 * UNORM formats (quantized to bytes on store) or any range for the float
 * formats; the runtime owns the float → storage encoding.
 *
 * **Raw-integer formats** (`R32I`/`R32UI`/`RGBA32I`/`RGBA32UI`) store 32-bit
 * signed/unsigned integers with **no** normalization or float conversion — the
 * texel read back IS the stored integer. They are **fetch-only**: the hardware
 * texture sampler cannot filter integer texels, so a `Texture2D<int32>` /
 * `Texture2D<uint32>` (the integer formats) supports `fetch` but not `sample`.
 * The texel type parameter `T` on `Texture2D<T>` selects whether a texture is
 * float- or integer-valued; pair the integer formats with `T = int32`/`uint32`.
 *
 * **Ordinal values are the stable native contract** — the
 * `__cajeta_xpu_texture_*` intrinsics (see
 * [`runtime/native/cajeta_runtime.c`](../../../native/cajeta_runtime.c)) switch
 * on them to pick the per-backend image format (`VK_FORMAT_*`, HIP
 * `hipChannelFormatDesc`, CPU storage). Do **not** reorder without updating that
 * C side.
 */
public enum TextureFormat {
    R32F,         // 0 — 1 channel, 32-bit float           (VK_FORMAT_R32_SFLOAT)
    R8_UNORM,     // 1 — 1 channel, 8-bit normalized [0,1]  (VK_FORMAT_R8_UNORM)
    RGBA8_UNORM,  // 2 — 4 channel, 8-bit normalized [0,1]  (VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM)
    RGBA32F,      // 3 — 4 channel, 32-bit float            (VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT)
    R16F,         // 4 — 1 channel, 16-bit half float       (VK_FORMAT_R16_SFLOAT)
    RGBA16F,      // 5 — 4 channel, 16-bit half float       (VK_FORMAT_R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT)
    R32I,         // 6 — 1 channel, 32-bit signed int       (VK_FORMAT_R32_SINT)    — fetch-only
    R32UI,        // 7 — 1 channel, 32-bit unsigned int     (VK_FORMAT_R32_UINT)    — fetch-only
    RGBA32I,      // 8 — 4 channel, 32-bit signed int       (VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_SINT)  — fetch-only
    RGBA32UI      // 9 — 4 channel, 32-bit unsigned int     (VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_UINT)  — fetch-only
}
